From 510177aec3bf53f27b8ccabc4f0a65b3a32f6450 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel <2660793+imDaniel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 12:33:49 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve JSON renderer depth in prompt text protection

Base: 1126 Attention fixes vLLM 44f3ee2ea2acd7aa70b12053c7f11d4d3d37c90c.

The tool protocol exposes decoded JSON before checking text for control
and image spellings. Recursing over the object can fail on a valid wire
argument the JSON codec and DSML renderer previously handled. Scan
strings lazily on an explicit stack. When a marker is present, rebuild
the request iteratively with its existing field, type and key semantics.

Quality: Ordinary deep JSON retains the release prompt and token IDs.
Known control and image spellings continue to use the text-only path.

Tests: CPU byte and real 1017 tokenizers exercise deep objects and arrays
with plain, control and literal image text through apply_chat_template.

Upstream status: Downstream candidate.
